+# Pre-Ship Review — USDC Payouts dApp (Base)
+
+Scope: `packages/nextjs` frontend + configuration, with a check of the deployed
+contract state on Base mainnet. Report only; no code was changed.
+
+`yarn next:check-types` passes, so nothing here is a compile error — every issue
+below is behavioral, configuration, or trust-signal.
+
+**Verdict: not shippable as-is.** 8 ship-blocking issues, 16 should-fix.
+
+---
+
+## Ship-blocking
+
+### 1. No contract exists at the Payouts address on Base mainnet
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:10`
+(`0x7c3f2A9d41B85E60Cf14a14e2b9D073A55e0b6F2`)
+
+`eth_getCode` for that address returns `0x` on three independent Base mainnet
+RPCs (`mainnet.base.org`, `base-rpc.publicnode.com`, `base.drpc.org`). The USDC
+address in the same file returns real bytecode, so this is not an RPC problem —
+the Payouts address is wrong, or the contract was never deployed to Base
+mainnet, or it was deployed to a different chain and the entry was hand-written.
+
+Every `pay()` call from real users will revert (call to an address with no
+code), and the event feed will always be empty. This is the single biggest
+blocker.
+
+**Fix:** redeploy to Base (`yarn deploy --network base`) and let hardhat-deploy
+regenerate `deployedContracts.ts`, or correct the address to the real deployment
+and confirm with `cast code <addr> --rpc-url https://mainnet.base.org`.
+
+### 2. Contract verification on Basescan is unconfirmed (and cannot be verified while #1 stands)
+
+**File:** `packages/hardhat/hardhat.config.ts:17`
+
+Verification could not be confirmed — there is no contract at the address to
+verify. Separately, `etherscanApiKey` falls back to the shared SE-2 demo key
+`DNXJA8RX2Q3VZ4URQIWP7Z68CJXQZSC6AW`, which is rate-limited and shared across
+every SE-2 user.
+
+**Fix:** after fixing #1, set a real `ETHERSCAN_API_KEY` in
+`packages/hardhat/.env` and run `yarn verify --network base`. Confirm the green
+checkmark on basescan.io before shipping.
+
+### 3. Raw wagmi `useWriteContract` instead of `useScaffoldWriteContract`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:21`
+
+`useWriteContract`'s `isPending` resolves the moment the wallet returns a tx
+hash, **not** when the transaction confirms. Combined with #4 this means the
+buttons re-enable while the approval is still mid-flight, and the user gets no
+transaction toast, no block-confirmation wait, and no explorer link.
+
+**Fix:** use `useScaffoldWriteContract({ contractName: "Payouts" })` and a
+second instance for `"USDC"`, calling `writeContractAsync({ functionName, args })`.
+That hook waits for confirmation and wires up the SE-2 transactor notifications.
+
+### 4. Approve and Send Payout are both visible and clickable simultaneously
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+Two primary buttons side by side, both enabled, sharing a single `isPending`
+flag. There is no allowance read anywhere on the page, so the UI cannot know
+whether approval is even needed. A user will click Send Payout first, eat a
+revert from `transferFrom`, see nothing (see #7), and retry. Users can also
+double-click Approve during the hash→confirmation window and sign two approvals.
+
+**Fix:** add `useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC", functionName:
+"allowance", args: [connectedAddress, PAYOUTS.address] })` and render exactly
+one button: Approve while `allowance < parsedAmount`, Send Payout otherwise.
+Gate the approve handler with both states from the QA checklist —
+`approvalSubmitting` (set at the top of the handler, cleared in `finally`) and
+`approveCooldown` (set after the await, cleared after ~4s plus
+`refetchAllowance()`) — and use `disabled={isPending || approvalSubmitting ||
+approveCooldown}`.
+
+### 5. "Please connect your wallet" text instead of a Connect button
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:70-71`
+
+The disconnected state is a paragraph. The only way to connect is the header
+button, which is not where the user is looking.
+
+**Fix:** render `<RainbowKitCustomConnectButton />` from
+`~~/components/scaffold-eth` as the primary CTA in the same slot the action
+buttons occupy.
+
+### 6. No wrong-network guard on the action buttons
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:99-114`
+
+A wallet connected to Ethereum mainnet, Arbitrum, or Optimism sees fully enabled
+Approve / Send Payout buttons. Clicking them fires against the wrong chain and
+fails with an opaque wagmi error. The header `WrongNetworkDropdown` is not a
+substitute — the user never looks up there mid-flow.
+
+**Fix:** branch the CTA slot on `useChainId() !== targetNetwork.id` and render a
+`useSwitchChain`-driven `Switch to Base` button in place of the action button.
+
+### 7. All transaction errors are swallowed to `console.error`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:44-46, 59-61`
+
+Both catch blocks log to the console and nothing else. A failed approval, a
+reverted `pay()` (`"Payouts: zero recipient"`, `"Payouts: zero amount"`,
+`"Payouts: transfer failed"` — i.e. insufficient balance or allowance), a
+rejected signature, or a wrong-chain error all look identical to the user:
+nothing happens. On a payouts app, "did my money move?" ambiguity is not
+acceptable.
+
+**Fix:** `import { notification, getParsedError } from "~~/utils/scaffold-eth"`
+and call `notification.error(getParsedError(e))` in each catch. Map the three
+contract require strings to plain English ("Recipient address is required",
+"Enter an amount above zero", "Not enough USDC — check your balance and
+approval"). Using `useScaffoldWriteContract` (#3) gives most of this for free.
+
+### 8. Default SE-2 branding ships to real users
+
+Four separate places, all still template:
+
+- `packages/nextjs/app/layout.tsx:11-12` — tab title is `Scaffold-ETH 2 App`,
+  description `Built with 🏗 Scaffold-ETH 2`.
+- `packages/nextjs/utils/scaffold-eth/getMetadata.ts:8` — every page title is
+  suffixed `| Scaffold-ETH 2`.
+- `packages/nextjs/components/Footer.tsx:50-74` — "Fork me" → scaffold-eth/se-2,
+  "Built with ♥ at BuidlGuidl", and a Telegram Support link that points at the
+  BuidlGuidl chat, not your team.
+- `README.md:1` — still the full Scaffold-ETH 2 template README.
+- `packages/nextjs/app/page.tsx:23-45` — the home page users land on says
+  "Welcome to Scaffold-ETH 2", "Get started by editing page.tsx", and references
+  `YourContract.sol`, a contract that does not exist in this repo.
+
+**Fix:** set title/description to the product name; change `titleTemplate` to
+`"%s | <App Name>"` or drop the template; strip the Fork me / BuidlGuidl /
+Support block from the footer (keep `SwitchTheme` and the price pill); rewrite
+the README for this project; replace the home page body with a real landing
+section, or redirect `/` to `/payouts`.
+
+---
+
+## Should-fix
+
+### 9. USDC registered inside the autogenerated `deployedContracts.ts`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/contracts/deployedContracts.ts:51` (USDC entry);
+`packages/nextjs/contracts/externalContracts.ts` is `{}`
+
+USDC is an external contract living in a file with a "do not edit manually,
+autogenerated" header. The next `yarn deploy` regenerates this file and silently
+deletes the USDC entry, breaking the balance read, the approve call, and
+`useScaffoldReadContract({ contractName: "USDC" })` everywhere.
+
+**Fix:** move the USDC entry verbatim into `externalContracts.ts` under key
+`8453`. Nothing else changes — the scaffold hooks merge both files.
+
+### 10. `pollingInterval: 30000` on an L2
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:24`
+
+Base produces a block every 2 seconds. A 30-second poll means a payout appears
+in the feed up to half a minute after it lands — the app looks broken or
+dropped the transaction.
+
+**Fix:** `pollingInterval: 3000`.
+
+### 11. Shipping on the shared default Alchemy key and WalletConnect project ID
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/scaffold.config.ts:29, 40`
+
+`alchemyApiKey` falls back to `DEFAULT_ALCHEMY_API_KEY` and
+`walletConnectProjectId` falls back to `3a8170812b534d0ff9d794f19a901d64`. Both
+are SE-2 demo credentials shared across every scaffold app; both are
+rate-limited. `.env.example` lists the variables but nothing confirms they are
+set on the hosting platform.
+
+**Fix:** provision your own Alchemy key and WalletConnect project, and verify
+they are actually present in the deploy environment (`vercel env ls`) — not just
+referenced in code. Consider setting `rpcOverrides: { [chains.base.id]: process.env.NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_RPC_URL }`
+with a dedicated Base endpoint.
+
+### 12. Bare `http()` fallback transport hits rate-limited public RPCs
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConfig.tsx:20`
+
+`rpcFallbacks` always includes a bare `http()`, which resolves to the chain's
+default public endpoint (`mainnet.base.org`). With the default Alchemy key in
+play the public RPC is ordered *first*, so normal traffic goes straight to the
+rate-limited endpoint.
+
+**Fix:** once a real RPC is configured (#11), drop the bare `http()` from the
+fallback list for Base so only intended transports are used.
+
+### 13. Raw text input for the recipient address
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:78-84`
+
+`<input type="text" placeholder="0x... recipient address">` with no validation.
+No ENS resolution, no blockie preview, no checksum check. Line 55 then casts the
+string straight to `` `0x${string}` `` — a typo'd or truncated address is sent
+to the contract as-is. On a payouts app this is how money goes to the wrong
+place.
+
+**Fix:** `<AddressInput value={recipient} onChange={setRecipient} placeholder="0x... or ENS name" />`
+from `@scaffold-ui/components`, and disable the action button while the value
+is not a valid address (`isAddress(recipient)`).
+
+### 14. The Payouts contract address is never shown
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx` (whole page)
+
+Users are approving USDC spend to a contract whose address appears nowhere in
+the UI. There is no way to check what they are approving.
+
+**Fix:** render `<Address address={PAYOUTS.address} chain={targetNetwork} />`
+near the header, labelled "Payouts contract".
+
+### 15. Hardcoded black background defeats the theme system
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:65`
+
+`className="min-h-screen bg-black text-white"` bypasses DaisyUI entirely. The
+`SwitchTheme` toggle in the footer does nothing on this page, and light-mode
+users get a black page inside an otherwise light shell. The feed rows at line
+121 have the same problem with `border-gray-700`.
+
+**Fix:** `className="min-h-screen bg-base-200 text-base-content"`, and
+`border-base-300` on the feed rows.
+
+### 16. DaisyUI `loading` class applied to the buttons
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:101, 108`
+
+`` className={`btn btn-primary ${isPending ? "loading" : ""}`} `` — DaisyUI's
+`loading` class on a `btn` replaces the button's entire content with a
+full-size spinner. The label disappears and the button looks broken.
+
+**Fix:** drop `loading` from the className and put the spinner inside:
+`{isPending && <span className="loading loading-spinner loading-sm mr-2" />}`
+alongside the label.
+
+### 17. `fromBlock: 0n` scans all of Base history on every mount
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:32`
+
+Base is past 30M blocks. With `watch: true` this triggers an enormous historical
+log scan on every page load — it will be slow, it will be rate-limited by the
+public RPC, and on many providers it will error outright and render an empty
+feed with no message.
+
+**Fix:** use the deployment block number (hardhat-deploy records it; also
+available in the deployment artifact under `packages/hardhat/deployments/base/`),
+e.g. `fromBlock: 21000000n`, as a named constant next to the contract import.
+
+### 18. Pill-shaped inputs from the SE-2 default `--radius-field`
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/styles/globals.css:36, 63`
+
+`--radius-field: 9999rem` in both theme blocks makes the amount input and
+especially the multi-line memo `<textarea>` render as capsules with clipped
+corners.
+
+**Fix:** set `--radius-field: 0.5rem` in both `@plugin "daisyui/theme"` blocks.
+Fix at theme level, not with per-input `rounded-*` classes.
+
+### 19. No USD value next to amounts
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:75, 85-91, 126`
+
+Balance, amount input, and feed entries show bare USDC figures. USDC is
+near-parity with the dollar so the stakes are lower than for a volatile token,
+but there is also no decimal formatting: `formatUnits(balance, 6)` renders
+`1234.567891` rather than `$1,234.57`.
+
+**Fix:** format to 2 decimals with thousands separators and prefix `$`, e.g.
+`Number(formatUnits(usdcBalance, 6)).toLocaleString("en-US", { style: "currency", currency: "USD" })`.
+
+### 20. Approval amount can silently drift from the payout amount
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:42 vs 55`
+
+`handleApprove` approves exactly `amount`. If the user approves 100, then edits
+the field to 250 and clicks Send Payout, the transfer reverts on allowance with
+no explanation (compounded by #7 and the missing allowance read in #4).
+
+**Fix:** with the allowance read from #4 in place, the Approve button naturally
+reappears when `allowance < parsedAmount`. Also clear/re-check allowance on
+amount change.
+
+### 21. No balance or amount validation before submitting
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:85-91, 107-113`
+
+`parseUnits(amount || "0", 6)` sends 0 when the field is empty, which the
+contract rejects with `"Payouts: zero amount"` — a wasted gas estimation and a
+confusing failure. Nothing checks the amount against `usdcBalance` either.
+
+**Fix:** disable Send Payout unless `parsedAmount > 0n && parsedAmount <= usdcBalance`,
+and surface "Amount exceeds your balance" inline.
+
+### 22. Phantom missing from the wallet list
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/services/web3/wagmiConnectors.tsx:20-28`
+
+Phantom has a large Base user base and is not in the SE-2 default list, so
+those users simply cannot connect.
+
+**Fix:** import `phantomWallet` from `@rainbow-me/rainbowkit/wallets` and add it
+to `wallets`. While there, set `appName` on line 49 from `"scaffold-eth-2"` to
+the real app name — it shows in the WalletConnect approval sheet.
+
+### 23. No mobile wallet deep linking
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:36-62`
+
+RainbowKit v2 / WalletConnect v2 does not auto-foreground the wallet app. On
+mobile, tapping Approve or Send Payout leaves the user on a spinner with no
+indication they must manually switch to their wallet — they will assume it hung
+and tap again.
+
+**Fix:** add a `writeAndOpen` helper that fires the write first and then
+`setTimeout(openWallet, 2000)`, wrapping **both** write calls. Detect the wallet
+from `connector?.id`/`name`, `localStorage["wagmi.recentConnectorId"]`, *and*
+the `wc@2:client…` localStorage session blob, and skip the deep link entirely
+when `window.ethereum` exists (already inside a wallet's in-app browser).
+
+### 24. Feed uses array index as React key and is unordered/unbounded
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/app/payouts/page.tsx:120-129`
+
+`key={i}` on a `watch: true` list that prepends new events causes React to
+reuse rows incorrectly as events arrive. The list is also unsorted (no explicit
+newest-first) and uncapped, and `shorten()` (line 13) hand-rolls address
+truncation instead of using the `<Address/>` component.
+
+**Fix:** key on `` `${log.transactionHash}-${log.logIndex}` ``, slice to the
+most recent ~25, sort newest-first, and replace `shorten()` with
+`<Address address={...} size="sm" />` to get blockies, ENS, copy, and explorer
+links.
+
+### 25. Debug Contracts tab ships in the production nav
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/components/Header.tsx:30-31`
+
+`/debug` is a developer tool that exposes every contract function, including
+any privileged ones, as a one-click form to end users. It is scaffolding, not
+product surface.
+
+**Fix:** drop the entry from `menuLinks` for production, or gate it on
+`targetNetwork.id === hardhat.id`.
+
+### 26. Favicon and OG thumbnail are the stock SE-2 assets
+
+**File:** `packages/nextjs/public/favicon.png`, `packages/nextjs/public/thumbnail.jpg`
+(referenced from `getMetadata.ts:13, 53`)
+
+Both are unchanged template assets, so shared links unfurl with the
+Scaffold-ETH thumbnail and the tab shows the SE-2 icon.
+
+**Fix:** replace both files with project artwork. Also confirm
+`VERCEL_PROJECT_PRODUCTION_URL` is set in the deploy environment — `getMetadata`
+falls back to `http://localhost:3000` for `metadataBase`, which would make every
+OG image URL point at localhost and break unfurling entirely.
+
+---
+
+## Verified-clean
+
+- `yarn next:check-types` — exit 0, no type errors.
+- `externalContracts.ts` is untouched template (empty), so nothing was
+  mis-registered there — the problem is the opposite (#9).
+- The USDC address `0x833589fCD6eDb6E08f4c7C32D4f71b54bdA02913` is correct for
+  Base mainnet and has bytecode onchain.
+- `Payouts.sol` itself is sound for USDC: the `require` on `transferFrom`'s
+  return value is correct, and the zero-address / zero-amount guards are present.

